Adds the single-segment (β.numSegs = 1) two-sided partition theorem with
conclusion `∃ U V, IsTwoSidedPartition (regionMinusArc R β.toSimpleArc) U V`,
choosing δ₀ and ρ internally.  For one segment there are no vertex sectors, so
the multi-segment endpoint-cap radius contradiction (cap-to-band reach needs
foot = 2α while cap-to-sector disjointness needs foot < α) never arises.

Disjointness of the two collar sides is proved DIRECTLY by side-separation:
collarPlus ⊆ {0 < sideForm s t} and collarMinus ⊆ {sideForm s t < 0} (every
band/end-cap piece carries the lone segment's half-plane sign; the sector union
is empty), via the two new helper lemmas
collarPlus_subset_pos_sideForm_of_numSegs_one /
collarMinus_subset_neg_sideForm_of_numSegs_one.

Kernel-clean axiom closure (propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound — no sorryAx):
the general P2-union lemma union_collarPlus_collarMinus carries a pre-existing
sorry in its interior-vertex disk branch, which would taint anything routed
through the standard entry point.  To stay sorry-free, this adds
union_collarPlus_collarMinus_of_numSegs_one (PLArc) — a verbatim copy whose
vacuous disk branch (no 0 < j < 1) is closed by omega — and a matching clean
entry point exists_twoSidedPartition_regionMinus_polyArc_of_collar_with_collar_sides_of_numSegs_one
(PLC).  P5 preconnectedness is discharged via the sorry-free sliver-budget
collar theorems in PLArc.

δ₀ := min(L(1-2α)/3, (α/2)·dotp/sum, mR/2), ρ ≡ (δ₀ + 2αL + L)/2 with
L = dist (segSrc firstSeg) (segTgt firstSeg).

Build: PLArc / PLCollarSeparation / CrossingLemma all green (LAKE_EXIT=0).

